{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 0d46e9933c02f2b1a392c772a975b47ab84031ef on builder/nf10-device-binding-origin-20261117, all 6 artifacts, for request 9431926b under my promise 0ba16609. The implementation is NF-10 (request e08158be, promise 84bbf5a1). The reporting artifact is the NF-10 note.\n\nThe head's parent is NF-9 head 6e9acc3a, which main 5ea5954f merges with an equal tree. `git merge-tree --write-tree 5ea5954f 0d46e993` gives fa7d964f, which is the head's own tree, so the landing merges cleanly with that tree.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- The note first, then the whole diff.\n- `device-key.ts`. `deviceSigner(device, origin)` checks the binding against the given origin instead of `location.origin`. The `binding` check itself does not change: the binding's origin must equal the given origin exactly, with no path, query, fragment or credentials, and with an http or https scheme. `imported` passes `identity.origin` after `importDemoBundle` or `importLegacyDevice` has already checked that identity against the caller's origin. The check there now only proves the key, which matches what it did before.\n- `storage.ts`. `privateDeviceStore(origin, installed)` passes the origin to `checkedDevices` on load and on save. The IndexedDB keys stay per installed scope.\n- `main.ts`. `serviceOrigin` is `screen?.origin ?? location.origin`. The device store, `mountDevice` and the demo-file import all use it.\n- Callers. `git grep` finds no other caller of the Counter `deviceSigner` or `privateDeviceStore`. Lending's `deviceSigner` in `examples/lending/browser/join.ts` is a separate function with no origin check, and `examples/lending/browser/main.ts` already binds to `screen?.origin ?? location.origin`, as the note states.\n- `release-identifiers.json` moves the open Counter 0.6.0 presentation from `76ad09f8` to `905a3f7e`. Counter 0.6.0 is unsigned, so ruling 163de663 allows the move.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- The red. `2026-11-17-nf10-red/red-device-binding-page-origin.txt` runs the new case against the check on `location.origin`. It fails 1 case, passes 57, and the failure is \"The device binding must belong to this origin.\"\n- The gate. END 2f8e9045 passed at this head. The last lines of `gate.txt` read \"gate passed\" and \"exit=0\".\n- Scope. The 6 artifacts name the head, no path repeats, and their paths equal the diff from 6e9acc3a and from 5ea5954f.\n- Cheap checks against base 6e9acc3a. The commit-message check passes: 1 checked, 0 flagged. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n- Wake rate. The head adds no alarm, retry or scheduled pass.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The fact belongs where the note puts it. The screen context names the service origin, invitations match that origin, and `applicationDeviceIdentity` builds the binding from it. The Counter's device check was the one place that used the page host instead. Each binding is now checked against the origin that made it, and the demo page keeps `location.origin` because it serves the room and the page from one origin.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding.\n\n- The check is no weaker. A binding must still name exactly one expected origin, and the new test refuses both the page's own origin and a third origin.\n- The expected origin comes from the screen context, which the page loads from its own screen host. The same value already selects where invitations, transports and request custody go, so a device signs only for the service it was enrolled with.\n- Device storage stays keyed by the installed scope on the screen host. A second installed screen on the same host keeps its own devices.\n\nSimplification: no required change.\n\nFacts for the planner: the hosted fix reaches users only through the five steps in the note, starting with a Counter 0.6.0 signing from main after this landing. The signed 0.6.0 presentation must equal `905a3f7e` unless another Counter page change lands first.\n\nThis approval authorizes no push, landing, signing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:35e3ccc9bf98736455b82f5e86cc1800bc49f31a","binding":"assigned","head":"0d46e9933c02f2b1a392c772a975b47ab84031ef","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0ba1660910dffdb0838f7faf598a8381e610e20d\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:84bbf5a12b4b069a248f555dc5e1ddd210573828\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0ba1660910dffdb0838f7faf598a8381e610e20d","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}